{{also|lëft}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|Left}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewbʰ-|id=cut off}}
From {{inh|en|enm|left}}, {{m|enm|luft}}, {{m|enm|leoft}}, {{m|enm|lift}}, {{m|enm|lyft}}, from {{inh|en|ang|left}}, {{m|ang|lyft|t=weak, clumsy, foolish}}, attested in {{cog|ang|lyftādl|t=palsy, paralysis}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*luft-}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*lubjaną|t=to castrate, lop off}} (compare dialectal {{cog|en|lib}}, {{cog|fy|lobje}}, {{cog|nl|lubben}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)lewp-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)lup-|t=hanging limply}}. Compare {{cog|sco|left|t=left}}, {{cog|frr|lefts}}, {{m|frr|leeft}}, {{m|frr|leefts|t=left}}, {{cog|fy|lofts|t=left}}, dialectal {{cog|nl|loof|t=weak, worthless}}, {{cog|nds|lucht|t=left}}.

