===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|left}}, variant of {{m|enm|laft|t=remaining, left}}, from {{inh|en|ang|læfd|lǣfd, ġelǣfd}}, past participle of {{m|ang|lǣfan|t=to leave}}. More at [[leave]].

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{en-past of|leave||depart, separate from; (cause or allow to) remain}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913|author={{w|Joseph C. Lincoln}}|chapter=8
|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5535161W Mr. Pratt's Patients]
|passage=Afore we got to the shanty Colonel Applegate stuck his head out of the door. His temper had been getting raggeder all the time, and the sousing he got when he fell overboard had just about ripped what was '''left''' of it to ravellings.}}
#: {{ux|en|There's not much food '''left'''.}}

